# Plain Google base, 80-column lines, left-aligned pointers, preserved include
# blocks. The Cpp section matches volumetric_kit_recon's and
# volumetric_kit_gfx's byte for byte, so all three siblings format C++
# identically.
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: Google
ColumnLimit: 80
IncludeBlocks: Preserve
DerivePointerAlignment: false
PointerAlignment: Left
---
# Objective-C++ is this repo's own concern -- it is where the .mm bridge onto
# the C++ libraries lives, and the siblings have no Objective-C at all. A config
# with only a Cpp section does not merely fall back for .mm files;
# clang-format refuses them outright ("Configuration file(s) do(es) not support
# Objective-C"), so this section is required, not cosmetic.
#
# Settings mirror the Cpp section so a file reads consistently across the
# language boundary, plus the Objective-C-only knobs pinned explicitly rather
# than derived from the file -- the same reason DerivePointerAlignment is
# pinned above.
Language: ObjC
BasedOnStyle: Google
ColumnLimit: 80
IncludeBlocks: Preserve
DerivePointerAlignment: false
PointerAlignment: Left
ObjCBlockIndentWidth: 2
ObjCSpaceAfterProperty: false
ObjCSpaceBeforeProtocolList: true
